# What never reaches a build context, and why the list is short.
#
# The server image copies four things — `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`,
# `CONTEXT.md` and `src/` — so most of this repository would be sent to the
# daemon, read once, and ignored. The entries below are the ones that would
# either be large, or would change on every run and so invalidate the cache for
# a reason that has nothing to do with the image.
#
# `.git/` is first for both reasons at once.
.git/
.github/
.claude/

# Materialised environments and tool caches. The image builds its own from the
# lockfile, and a host's `.venv/` is the wrong platform anyway.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Proof artifacts and prose. Neither is in the image: the suites run against a
# running server from outside it, and the ADR trail is read in a browser.
tests/
docs/
keycloak/
db/
public/
